---
// The hooks that FairRunAna calls on a tree of tasks, step by step.
// Facts (current FairRoot code):
// - FairRun makes the main task fTask = new FairTask("FairTaskList"). AddTask() adds a task to it
//   (fairroot/base/steer/FairRun.cxx:45, 110-114). A task holds its subtasks in the TTask list.
// - The macro calls fRun->AddTask(), fRun->Init() and fRun->Run()
//   (examples/simulation/Tutorial2/macros/create_digis.C:77-94).
// - FairRunAna::Init() calls fTask->SetParTask() (FairRunAna.cxx:201 or 209), then
//   fRtdb->initContainers(fRunId) (220), then fTask->InitTask() (238). With an input file, one more
//   initContainers() comes before SetParTask() (198); the call in line 220 always comes after it.
//   The run ID comes from the event header of the input (186-191), or FairRunIdGenerator makes one (205-208).
//   FairFileSource::SpecifyRunId() reads entry 0 for it (fairroot/base/source/FairFileSource.cxx:300-304),
//   so event 0 has the run ID of Init().
// - SetParTask(): if the task is active, SetParContainers(), then SetParTask() of each subtask
//   (FairTask.cxx:81-88, 220-228). A task requests its containers there with getContainer(); they are
//   not filled yet (FairRuntimeDb.cxx:199-218, Tutorial2/src/FairTutorialDet2Digitizer.cxx:39-51).
// - initContainers(runId) calls init() of each container that is not static (FairRuntimeDb.cxx:464-484, 508-564).
// - InitTask(): if active, Init(). kFATAL: LOG(fatal) << "Initialization of Task ... failed fatally".
//   kERROR: fActive = kFALSE. kSUCCESS: nothing changes. Then InitTask() of each subtask
//   (FairTask.cxx:49-64, 118-126). The default Init() returns kSUCCESS (FairTask.h:29-34, 116).
//   LOG(fatal) calls the fatal callback of FairLogger, if one is set (FairLogger Logger.cxx, ~Logger()). The
//   constructor of FairRoot's FairLogger class (FairLogger::GetLogger(), gLogger) sets one that throws
//   fair::FatalException (fairroot/tools/FairLogger.cxx:28-38, 179-202); without it, the run continues.
//   So the diagram says LOG(fatal), not "the run stops".
// - Run() without arguments processes all entries of the input (FairRunAna.h:43, FairRunAna.cxx:269-274).
//   For each event: ReadEvent(i), FillEventHeader(), CheckRunIdChanged(), ExecuteTask(""), Fill(),
//   FinishEvent() (FairRunAna.cxx:302-337).
// - CheckRunIdChanged(): a new run ID -> Reinit(fRunId), which calls fRtdb->initContainers(runId),
//   then fTask->ReInitTask(). With SetContainerStatic(kTRUE), neither (FairRunAna.cxx:568-592).
//   ReInitTask() handles the return value of ReInit() like InitTask() (FairTask.cxx:66-79, 210-218).
// - ExecuteTask(): Exec() of the task, then ExecuteTasks(): for each active subtask, Exec() and then its
//   own subtasks. So a task comes before its subtasks, and its subtasks before the next task. An inactive
//   task and its subtasks are skipped (FairTask.cxx:128-208).
// - Fill() -> FairRootManager::Fill() -> FairRootFileSink::Fill() -> fOutTree->Fill()
//   (FairRunAna.cxx:617-624, FairRootManager.cxx:331-335, FairRootFileSink.cxx:302-309). Init() makes the
//   output tree after InitTask() (FairRunAna.cxx:250, FairRootFileSink.cxx:238-249). Its default name is
//   cbmsim (FairRootManager.cxx:932-944). So the sink row appears with Run().
// - FinishEvent(): if active, FinishEvent() of each subtask (FairTask.cxx:90-96, 240-248). FinishEvent() is
//   itself the virtual hook: a task that overrides it must call FairTask::FinishEvent() to reach its subtasks.
// - After the loop: fTask->FinishTask(): if active, Finish(), then FinishTask() of each subtask; then
//   LastFill() and Write(); Write() writes the tree to the file (FairRunAna.cxx:339-345,
//   FairTask.cxx:98-105, 230-238, FairRootManager.cxx:346-356, FairRootFileSink.cxx:311-332).
// Example values, not from the code: the tasks A, A1 and B, the containers ParA, ParA1 and ParB, the
// run IDs 1 and 2, and the 6 events. A1 is a subtask of A (not of B): then the order A, A1, B shows that
// the order is depth first.
import Explainer from './Explainer.astro';

const steps = [
  {
    cap: 'The macro calls Init(). The run keeps the tasks under its main task, FairTaskList. AddTask() added A and B, and A has a subtask, A1.',
    code: 'fRun->Init();',
  },
  {
    cap: 'SetParTask() calls SetParContainers() on each task, in tree order: a task, then its subtasks, then the next task. Each task requests its parameter containers. The containers are still empty.',
    code: 'fTask->SetParTask();',
    set: { call: 'SetParTask()', hook: 'SetParContainers()', db: 'getContainer()' },
  },
  {
    cap: 'The runtime database fills the containers with the parameters for the run ID, so Init() can use them. The run ID comes from the input, or the run makes a new one.',
    code: 'fRtdb->initContainers(fRunId);',
    set: { db: 'initContainers(fRunId)', rid: 'run ID 1' },
  },
  {
    cap: 'InitTask() calls Init() on each task, in tree order. kSUCCESS keeps the task active. kERROR makes it inactive: the run calls no Exec() for it and its subtasks. kFATAL logs a message with the severity fatal.',
    code: 'fTask->InitTask();',
    set: { call: 'InitTask()', hook: 'Init()', rid: 'run ID 1' },
  },
  {
    cap: 'The macro calls Run(). The source reads one event at a time. Event 0 has the run ID of Init(), so the parameters stay the same.',
    code: 'fRootManager->ReadEvent(i);',
    set: { ev: 'i = 0', rid: 'run ID 1' },
  },
  {
    cap: 'ExecuteTask() calls Exec() on each active task, in tree order. Here the tasks do their work for the event.',
    code: 'fTask->ExecuteTask("");',
    set: { call: 'ExecuteTask("")', hook: 'Exec()', ev: 'i = 0', rid: 'run ID 1' },
  },
  {
    cap: 'The run writes the event to the output tree. Then it calls FinishEvent() on each task, in tree order.',
    code: 'fTask->FinishEvent();',
    set: { call: 'FinishEvent()', hook: 'FinishEvent()', ev: 'i = 0', rid: 'run ID 1' },
  },
  {
    cap: 'Events 1 and 2 go through the same steps. Event 3 has a new run ID, so the runtime database initializes the containers again. Then ReInitTask() calls ReInit() on each task.',
    code: 'fTask->ReInitTask();',
    set: { call: 'ReInitTask()', hook: 'ReInit()', db: 'initContainers(fRunId)', ev: 'i = 3', rid: 'run ID 2' },
  },
  {
    cap: 'After the last event, FinishTask() calls Finish() on each task, in tree order. Then the run writes the output tree to the file.',
    code: 'fTask->FinishTask();',
    set: { call: 'FinishTask()', hook: 'Finish()', ev: '6 events', rid: 'run ID 2' },
  },
];

// The tasks in tree order. n is the place in the call order.
const tasks = [
  { id: 'a', name: 'A', par: 'ParA', n: 1 },
  { id: 'a1', name: 'A1', par: 'ParA1', n: 2 },
  { id: 'b', name: 'B', par: 'ParB', n: 3 },
] as const;
type Id = (typeof tasks)[number]['id'];
type Box = [number, number, number, number];
type Layout = {
  k: 'd' | 'm';
  w: number;
  h: number;
  run: Box;
  ttl: [number, number];
  pill: { y: number; init: [number, number]; run: [number, number] };
  root: { y: number; x: number; w: number };
  rows: Record<Id, { y: number; x: number; w: number }>;
  edges: string[];
  badgeX: number;
  hookX: number;
  retR: number;
  db: { box: Box; ttl: [number, number]; rid: [number, number]; call: [number, number]; sub?: [number, number] };
  chips: Record<Id, Box>;
  link?: [number, number];
  // step: distance between two event cells. On the narrow stage, the six cells fill the width of the boxes.
  src: { label: [number, number]; ev: [number, number]; x0: number; cw: number; step: number; y: number; band: number; blbl: number };
  // wrEnd: Write() takes the place of the tree name (narrow stage), else it goes below the cells.
  out: { label: [number, number]; name: [number, number]; x0: number; y: number; wr: [number, number]; wrEnd?: boolean };
  legend: { kx: number; vx: number; head?: number; ys: [number, number, number] };
};
const CH = 26; // height of an event cell

// Wide stage.
const D: Layout = {
  k: 'd',
  w: 680,
  h: 296,
  run: [12, 10, 400, 186],
  ttl: [28, 37],
  pill: { y: 22, init: [274, 61], run: [342, 54] },
  root: { y: 76, x: 28, w: 112 },
  rows: { a: { y: 108, x: 52, w: 30 }, a1: { y: 140, x: 76, w: 36 }, b: { y: 172, x: 52, w: 30 } },
  edges: ['M40 88V172H52', 'M40 108H52', 'M67 120V140H76'],
  badgeX: 166,
  hookX: 192,
  retR: 396,
  db: { box: [428, 10, 240, 186], ttl: [444, 37], rid: [652, 37], call: [444, 80], sub: [444, 56] },
  chips: { a: [444, 96, 208, 24], a1: [444, 128, 208, 24], b: [444, 160, 208, 24] },
  link: [336, 437],
  src: { label: [12, 226], ev: [330, 226], x0: 12, cw: 48, step: 54, y: 234, band: 265, blbl: 282 },
  out: { label: [346, 226], name: [664, 226], x0: 346, y: 234, wr: [346, 282] },
  legend: { kx: 346, vx: 424, head: 226, ys: [248, 266, 284] },
};
// Narrow stage (phones): the same parts, stacked.
const M: Layout = {
  k: 'm',
  w: 340,
  h: 446,
  run: [6, 6, 328, 186],
  ttl: [18, 33],
  pill: { y: 19, init: [207, 58], run: [271, 51] },
  root: { y: 72, x: 18, w: 104 },
  rows: { a: { y: 104, x: 40, w: 28 }, a1: { y: 136, x: 62, w: 34 }, b: { y: 168, x: 40, w: 28 } },
  edges: ['M30 84V168H40', 'M30 104H40', 'M54 116V136H62'],
  badgeX: 106,
  hookX: 130,
  retR: 322,
  db: { box: [6, 202, 328, 86], ttl: [18, 226], rid: [322, 226], call: [18, 249] },
  chips: { a: [18, 258, 98, 22], a1: [121, 258, 98, 22], b: [224, 258, 98, 22] },
  src: { label: [6, 314], ev: [334, 314], x0: 6, cw: 50, step: 55.6, y: 322, band: 353, blbl: 370 },
  out: { label: [6, 398], name: [334, 398], x0: 6, y: 406, wr: [334, 398], wrEnd: true },
  legend: { kx: 6, vx: 82, ys: [398, 416, 434] },
};
const events = [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5];
const cx = (g: Layout, x0: number, k: number) => x0 + k * g.src.step + g.src.cw / 2;
---

<Explainer title="The hooks of a task, in order" meta="FairRunAna · 3 tasks · 6 events" steps={steps}>
  <div class="tl-wrap">
    <svg
      class="tl"
      data-stage
      role="img"
      aria-label="The run FairRunAna with its main task FairTaskList and the tasks A, A1 and B, the runtime database with the parameter containers, the source with 6 events and the sink with the output tree."
    >
      {
        [D, M].map((g) => (
          <svg class={`lay lay-${g.k}`} viewBox={`0 0 ${g.w} ${g.h}`} width="100%" height="100%">
            {/* the run and its task tree */}
            <rect class="box" x={g.run[0]} y={g.run[1]} width={g.run[2]} height={g.run[3]} rx="4" />
            <text class="ttl" x={g.ttl[0]} y={g.ttl[1]}>
              FairRunAna
            </text>
            <g class="pill p-init">
              <rect x={g.pill.init[0]} y={g.pill.y} width={g.pill.init[1]} height="22" rx="11" />
              <text x={g.pill.init[0] + g.pill.init[1] / 2} y={g.pill.y + 15} text-anchor="middle">
                Init()
              </text>
            </g>
            <g class="pill p-run">
              <rect x={g.pill.run[0]} y={g.pill.y} width={g.pill.run[1]} height="22" rx="11" />
              <text x={g.pill.run[0] + g.pill.run[1] / 2} y={g.pill.y + 15} text-anchor="middle">
                Run()
              </text>
            </g>
            {g.edges.map((d) => (
              <path class="edge" d={d} pathLength="1" />
            ))}
            <g class="row r0">
              <rect class="node" x={g.root.x} y={g.root.y - 12} width={g.root.w} height="24" rx="3" />
              <rect class="hl pass" x={g.root.x} y={g.root.y - 12} width={g.root.w} height="24" rx="3" />
              <text class="nname" x={g.root.x + g.root.w / 2} y={g.root.y + 4.5} text-anchor="middle">
                FairTaskList
              </text>
              <text class="call pass" x={g.hookX} y={g.root.y + 4.5} data-slot="call" />
            </g>
            {tasks.map((t) => {
              const p = g.rows[t.id];
              return (
                <g class={`row r-${t.id}`}>
                  <rect class="node" x={p.x} y={p.y - 12} width={p.w} height="24" rx="3" />
                  <rect class="hl pass" x={p.x} y={p.y - 12} width={p.w} height="24" rx="3" />
                  <text class="nname" x={p.x + p.w / 2} y={p.y + 4.5} text-anchor="middle">
                    {t.name}
                  </text>
                  <g class="badge pass">
                    <rect x={g.badgeX} y={p.y - 8.5} width="17" height="17" rx="2" />
                    <text x={g.badgeX + 8.5} y={p.y + 4} text-anchor="middle">
                      {t.n}
                    </text>
                  </g>
                  <text class="hook pass" x={g.hookX} y={p.y + 4.5} data-slot="hook" />
                  <g class="ret">
                    <rect x={g.retR - 70} y={p.y - 9} width="70" height="18" rx="9" />
                    <text x={g.retR - 35} y={p.y + 4} text-anchor="middle">
                      kSUCCESS
                    </text>
                  </g>
                  {g.link && (
                    <g class="link">
                      <path class="lk-line" d={`M${g.link[0]} ${p.y}H${g.link[1] - 6}`} />
                      <path class="lk-head" d={`M${g.link[1] - 7} ${p.y - 4}L${g.link[1]} ${p.y}L${g.link[1] - 7} ${p.y + 4}z`} />
                    </g>
                  )}
                </g>
              );
            })}

            {/* the runtime database */}
            <rect class="box" x={g.db.box[0]} y={g.db.box[1]} width={g.db.box[2]} height={g.db.box[3]} rx="4" />
            <rect class="dbhl" x={g.db.box[0]} y={g.db.box[1]} width={g.db.box[2]} height={g.db.box[3]} rx="4" />
            <text class="ttl" x={g.db.ttl[0]} y={g.db.ttl[1]}>
              FairRuntimeDb
            </text>
            {g.db.sub && (
              <text class="sub" x={g.db.sub[0]} y={g.db.sub[1]}>
                parameter containers
              </text>
            )}
            <text class="rid" x={g.db.rid[0]} y={g.db.rid[1]} text-anchor="end" data-slot="rid" />
            <text class="dbcall" x={g.db.call[0]} y={g.db.call[1]} data-slot="db" />
            {tasks.map((t) => {
              const [x, y, w, h] = g.chips[t.id];
              return (
                <g class={`chip c-${t.id}`}>
                  <rect class="bar1" x={x} y={y} width={w} height={h} rx="3" />
                  <rect class="bar2" x={x} y={y} width={w} height={h} rx="3" />
                  <rect class="cfr" x={x} y={y} width={w} height={h} rx="3" />
                  <text class="clbl" x={x + 9} y={y + h / 2 + 4.2}>
                    {t.par}
                  </text>
                  <text class="empty" x={x + w - 8} y={y + h / 2 + 4} text-anchor="end">
                    empty
                  </text>
                </g>
              );
            })}

            {/* the source with its events */}
            <text class="sub" x={g.src.label[0]} y={g.src.label[1]}>
              source
            </text>
            <text class="ev" x={g.src.ev[0]} y={g.src.ev[1]} text-anchor="end" data-slot="ev" />
            {events.map((k) => (
              <g class={`cell e${k}`}>
                <rect class="cbg" x={g.src.x0 + k * g.src.step} y={g.src.y} width={g.src.cw} height={CH} rx="3" />
                <rect class="cfr2" x={g.src.x0 + k * g.src.step} y={g.src.y} width={g.src.cw} height={CH} rx="3" />
                <text class="cnum" x={cx(g, g.src.x0, k)} y={g.src.y + 17.5} text-anchor="middle">
                  {k}
                </text>
              </g>
            ))}
            <rect
              class="cur"
              x={g.src.x0 - 2.5}
              y={g.src.y - 2.5}
              width={g.src.cw + 5}
              height={CH + 5}
              rx="4"
              style={`--to3: ${3 * g.src.step}px`}
            />
            <rect class="band b1" x={g.src.x0} y={g.src.band} width={2 * g.src.step + g.src.cw} height="3" />
            <rect class="band b2" x={g.src.x0 + 3 * g.src.step} y={g.src.band} width={2 * g.src.step + g.src.cw} height="3" />
            <text class="blbl b1t" x={cx(g, g.src.x0, 1)} y={g.src.blbl} text-anchor="middle">
              run ID 1
            </text>
            <text class="blbl b2t" x={cx(g, g.src.x0, 4)} y={g.src.blbl} text-anchor="middle">
              run ID 2
            </text>

            {/* the sink with the output tree */}
            <g class="outrow">
              <text class="sub" x={g.out.label[0]} y={g.out.label[1]}>
                sink
              </text>
              <text class={g.out.wrEnd ? 'sub swap' : 'sub'} x={g.out.name[0]} y={g.out.name[1]} text-anchor="end">
                tree cbmsim
              </text>
              {events.map((k) => (
                <g class={`oc o${k}`}>
                  <rect class="ofr" x={g.out.x0 + k * g.src.step} y={g.out.y} width={g.src.cw} height={CH} rx="3" />
                  <rect class="ofill" x={g.out.x0 + k * g.src.step + 3} y={g.out.y + 3} width={g.src.cw - 6} height={CH - 6} rx="2" />
                </g>
              ))}
            </g>
            <text class="wr" x={g.out.wr[0]} y={g.out.wr[1]} text-anchor={g.out.wrEnd ? 'end' : 'start'}>
              Write() → output file
            </text>

            {/* what InitTask() does with the return value of Init() */}
            <g class="legend">
              {g.legend.head && (
                <text class="sub" x={g.legend.kx} y={g.legend.head}>
                  Init() returns
                </text>
              )}
              <text class="lk ok" x={g.legend.kx} y={g.legend.ys[0]}>
                kSUCCESS
              </text>
              <text class="lv" x={g.legend.vx} y={g.legend.ys[0]}>
                the task stays active
              </text>
              <text class="lk bad" x={g.legend.kx} y={g.legend.ys[1]}>
                kERROR
              </text>
              <text class="lv" x={g.legend.vx} y={g.legend.ys[1]}>
                inactive: no Exec()
              </text>
              <text class="lk bad" x={g.legend.kx} y={g.legend.ys[2]}>
                kFATAL
              </text>
              <text class="lv" x={g.legend.vx} y={g.legend.ys[2]}>
                LOG(fatal)
              </text>
            </g>
          </svg>
        ))
      }
    </svg>
  </div>
</Explainer>

<style>
  /* Two layouts in one stage: the wide one, and a narrow one when the stage is narrow. */
  .tl-wrap {
    container-type: inline-size;
  }
  .tl {
    aspect-ratio: 680 / 296;
  }
  .lay-m {
    display: none;
  }
  @container (max-width: 579px) {
    .tl {
      aspect-ratio: 340 / 446;
      max-width: 440px;
      margin-inline: auto;
    }
    .lay-d {
      display: none;
    }
    .lay-m {
      display: inline;
    }
  }

  /* Parts */
  .box {
    fill: var(--fr-stage-2);
    stroke: var(--fr-stage-line);
    stroke-width: 1.2;
  }
  .ttl {
    fill: var(--fr-stage-ink);
    font-size: 14.5px;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .sub {
    fill: var(--fr-stage-dim);
    font-size: 12px;
  }
  .pill rect {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--fr-stage-line);
    stroke-width: 1.2;
    transition:
      fill 0.4s,
      stroke 0.4s;
  }
  .pill text {
    fill: var(--fr-stage-dim);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 600;
    transition: fill 0.4s;
  }
  .edge {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--fr-stage-line);
    stroke-width: 1.2;
    stroke-dasharray: 1;
  }
  .node {
    fill: var(--fr-stage);
    stroke: var(--fr-stage-line);
    stroke-width: 1.2;
  }
  .nname {
    fill: var(--fr-stage-ink);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .hl {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--fr-saffron);
    stroke-width: 2;
  }
  .call {
    fill: var(--fr-stage-ink);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .hook {
    fill: var(--fr-saffron);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .badge rect {
    fill: var(--fr-saffron);
  }
  .badge text {
    fill: var(--fr-on-saffron);
    font-size: 11.5px;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .ret rect {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--fr-mint);
    stroke-width: 1.2;
  }
  .ret text,
  .lk.ok {
    fill: var(--fr-mint);
    font-size: 11.5px;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .lk-line {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--fr-sky-bright);
    stroke-width: 1.4;
    stroke-dasharray: 4 3;
  }
  .lk-head {
    fill: var(--fr-sky-bright);
  }
  .dbhl {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--fr-saffron);
    stroke-width: 2;
  }
  .dbcall,
  .ev {
    fill: var(--fr-saffron);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .rid {
    fill: var(--fr-sky-bright);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 700;
    transition: fill 0.4s;
  }
  .cfr {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--fr-stage-line);
    stroke-width: 1.2;
    stroke-dasharray: 3 3;
    transition: stroke 0.3s;
  }
  .bar1,
  .bar2 {
    transform-box: fill-box;
    transform-origin: left center;
    transform: scaleX(0);
    transition: transform 0.7s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0, 0.1, 1);
  }
  /* Opaque tints, so that the values of run ID 2 cover the values of run ID 1. */
  .bar1 {
    fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fr-sky-bright) 26%, var(--fr-stage-2));
  }
  .bar2 {
